  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": "Mix components and autoclave under a N2 gas atmosphere."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": "Mix components and autoclave under a N2 atmosphere."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 10,
      "comment": "Mix components, filter--sterilize and store under a N2--CO2 (4:1, v/v) gas mixture."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 11,
      "comment": "To complete the medium, combine Solutions A, B, C and 1 ml Vitamin solution (see below) aseptically under a stream of a N2--CO2 (4:1, v/v) gas mixture. Distribute the medium into sterilized culture vessels under the same gas mixture and seal with butyl rubber stoppers. Then, add 0.01 volume of 5% Na2S・9H2O solution (autoclaved under a N2 atmosphere). Check the final pHto be 7.0 -- 7.2. Pressurize the inoculated vessels to 70 kPa N2--CO2 (4:1, v/v) overpressure."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 14,
      "comment": "Filter--sterilize and store under a N2 atmosphere."
    }
  ]
}